 "notes": [
  "Circuit per the manual: MIDI jack pin 5 -> 220 ohm -> Arduino digital pin 1 (TX); pin 2 -> GND; pin 4 -> 220 ohm -> +5V.",
  "The breadboard image shows the MIDI jack mounted on the top half with three legs in columns 7, 8 and 9 (left yellow = pin 5, middle black = pin 2, right red = pin 4). I put the jack legs in the catalogue's 'b' bank (rows f-j) and the resistors across the centre gap into the 't' bank. The exact row letters are approximate.",
  "The image shows the 'manual' parts list as 1 hook-up wire, but the circuit uses three jumper wires (yellow TX, red 5V, black GND).",
  "The black wire goes to the GND header next to AREF on the digital side. I assumed this is GND.3, since the catalogue doesn't say which GND header pin that is.",
  "The manual's resistors are 220 ohm; the catalogue resistor is named 100 ohm, so each resistor has value=220.",
  "The jack's pins 1 and 3 are not connected."
